// @no-instantiate expected
// ACCEPTS, THEN MISCOMPILES. An EMPTY array literal annotated with a NUMERIC literal-union
// element type: `vl check --codegen` exits 0 and the module does not validate.
//
//     type K = 1.5 | 2.5
//     const xs: K[] = []        // type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// THREE CONTROLS place it, all in `literal-unions/numeric-litunion-list-seed-controls.vl`:
// the same annotation with a NON-empty literal compiles and runs; the STRING literal-union
// spelling with an empty literal compiles and runs; and a plain `f64[] = []` compiles and runs.
// It is the pair — numeric literal-union element AND an empty literal.
//
// THE ROOT IS ONE PREDICATE, and it is the same one behind two other filed gaps.
// `tyAnnRefListKind`'s first structural arm is `tyIsLitUnionArray(nodeTyIxOf(tyIx))`, which seeds
// NO list kind so an empty `[]` builds the default wrapper rather than a string list. It answers
// only for STRING literal unions: `tyIsLitUnion` demands `litKind == "str"`, so a numeric member
// set matches nothing and the node falls past the arm into the name rungs below, where the canon
// pass's softened spelling picks a wrapper the cell is not.
//
// The same `litKind == "str"` restriction produced the two other numeric-litunion gaps on file:
// `xfail-false-reject-numeric-litunion-array-in-signature.vl` (a `K[]` in a function signature is
// refused outright), and the `collectA` rungs repaired in #1563, where a covered node whose
// element is a `TyUnion` of numeric `TyLit`s left `nodeTyArrayElemRepName` answering `""`.
//
// NOT FIXED HERE because the fix is not a fallback. Teaching this arm the numeric case means
// deciding what a numeric literal-union list's REP is — its members are f64 (or i64) values, not
// interned i32 atoms, so it wants a scalar-list wrapper and not the string-litunion treatment.
// That is a feature decision about the numeric literal-union family, not a destringify slice, and
// guessing it here would trade a loud shape for a quiet one.
//
// WHEN IT CLOSES: drop the prefix, flip to `@run`, assert `0` from `xs.length`.
type K = 1.5 | 2.5

const xs: K[] = []
print(xs.length)
